BT /F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 706.80 Tm (3. What this means in practice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 680.40 Tm (Patients whose most recent potassium measurement falls within the new interval) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 667.20 Tm (require no immediate action; they move onto the shorter schedule from their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 654.00 Tm (next measurement. Patients whose most recent measurement is older than the new) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 640.80 Tm (interval should have one arranged.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 614.40 Tm (The Committee wishes to be explicit on one point: this revision is not a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 601.20 Tm (statement that previously compliant care was substandard. It is a change to a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 588.00 Tm (threshold in light of new operating data, and it should be communicated to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 574.80 Tm (patients in those terms if the question arises.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 548.40 Tm (4. Scope unchanged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 522.00 Tm (The population remains as defined in SAFETY_DOC_007 - CardioZen recipients) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 508.80 Tm (with a diagnosis of chronic kidney disease. This memorandum makes no change) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 495.60 Tm (for patients without that diagnosis, and introduces no requirement for any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 482.40 Tm (test other than serum potassium.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 456.00 Tm (5. Status of SAFETY_DOC_007) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 429.60 Tm (SAFETY_DOC_007 should be treated as superseded in respect of the monitoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 416.40 Tm (interval in its section 3. Its remaining sections stand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.0 Tf 1 0 0 1 62 390.00 Tm (- Ends -) Tj ET
